4. HEALTH AND SAFETY. READ THIS SECTION.

Feeziq is a fitness and wellness tool. It is not a medical device, not
a healthcare provider, and not a substitute for professional advice.
Nothing in the app is a diagnosis, a treatment, a prescription or
medical advice.

- Consult a qualified clinician before starting any exercise or diet
  programme, and especially if you are pregnant or postpartum, have a
  heart condition, high blood pressure, diabetes, an eating disorder or
  a history of one, an injury, or any chronic condition, or if you take
  medication of any kind.
- Stop exercising immediately and seek medical help if you feel chest
  pain, dizziness, faintness, breathlessness beyond normal exertion, or
  pain that is sharp rather than muscular.
- Calorie, macronutrient, hydration and MET values in Feeziq are
  estimates. Estimates produced by AI from a photo or a written
  description are approximations and are often wrong in detail. Do not
  rely on them for any clinical purpose, and do not use them to manage a
  medical condition.
- You decide what you do with your body. You accept the risks inherent
  in physical exercise and in changing your diet, and you exercise and
  eat at your own risk.
- Feeziq is not appropriate for the treatment of eating disorders. Its
  calorie tracking, streaks and weight logging can be harmful in that
  context. If you are struggling, please stop using the app and speak to
  a professional.


